TITLE:: LegatoCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that sets legato on selected piano-roll notes and updates their sounding duration.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/PlayableNote

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::LegatoCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::legato:: that writes CODE::\legato:: onto selected LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: instances and updates each wrapped LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: stop time. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes and loop bound through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes:: and CODE::loopEnd::.

CODE::values:: is a space-separated list of LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::s greater than CODE::0::. Values greater than CODE::1:: are allowed. The Event key is stored as given, with no clipping or mapping. Notes are ordered by CODE::startTime:: only. Notes that share a start time take the same array value; the list wraps and advances only when start time changes.

Sounding duration is a proportion of the inter-onset interval: CODE::stopTime = startTime + (nextOnset - startTime) * legato::. CODE::nextOnset:: is the next distinct start time in the selection. For the last group, CODE::nextOnset:: is CODE::loopEnd::.

Example: four notes at beats CODE::0, 1, 1, 2:: with CODE::loopEnd:: CODE::4:: and CODE::legato values 0.5:: become stop times CODE::0.5, 1.5, 1.5, 3::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::LegatoCommand::. Takes no arguments; legato is applied by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::LegatoCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: execute
Applies wrapped legato values to CODE::\selectedNotes:: grouped by start time, writing CODE::\legato:: and updating stop times from each group's next onset (or CODE::\loopEnd::).

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes that respond to CODE::legato_::), CODE::\loopEnd:: (a LINK::Classes/Number::), and CODE::\values:: (a non-empty LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::s greater than CODE::0::).

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var notes = [0, 1, 1, 2].collect({
	|start, i|
	var note = PianoRollNote(start, 60 + i, 100,
		viewFunc: { View() },
		selectFunc: {},
		deselectFunc: {},
		setPart1Func: {},
		setPart2Func: {},
		setPart3Func: {},
		setPart4Func: {},
		moveFunc: {}
	);
	note.stop(start + 1.0);
	note;
});
LegatoCommand.new.execute((
	selectedNotes: notes,
	loopEnd: 4,
	values: [0.5]
));
)
::
